<title>DUBAI: Lebanon gets $50 mln soft loan from Abu Dhabi.</title>
<headline>Lebanon gets $50 mln soft loan from Abu Dhabi.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Abu Dhabi Development Fund (ADF) has pledged a 185 million dirham ($50 million) soft loan to Lebanon as part of an aid package, the official WAM news agency said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>WAM said the pledge was made at a conference in Washington this week. The agency, which did not give details of the loan, said it based its report on comments by ADF's director general Saeed Mohammad al-Mazroui.</p>
<p>Delegates from 30 countries and financial institutions took part in the conference, pledging more than $3 billion in immediate and long-term aid to help Lebanon recover from a 16-year civil war.</p>
<p>No official breakdown was available of who was donating the aid.</p>
</text>
